.TH ARC-DGPU-CTL 8 "" "arc-dgpu-ctl" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
arc-dgpu-ctl \- power off / on an Intel Arc (Alchemist) discrete GPU at runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arc-dgpu-ctl
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arc-dgpu-ctl
unbinds the HDA audio companion and the i915/xe driver of an Intel Arc
Alchemist (DG2) GPU in a safe order and removes both from the PCI bus, so the
PCIe root port can enter D3cold. It restores the GPU without a reboot.
.PP
Mobile Arc (A350M\(enA770M) is supported. Desktop A380, A580, A750 and A770
are supported only when every display is connected to the CPU's integrated
GPU. Other Alchemist models require \fBALLOW_UNSUPPORTED=1\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
State, model, bound drivers, PCIe port power states and power draw (default).
.TP
.B state
Print exactly \fBon\fR or \fBoff\fR. Machine-readable; for other programs.
.TP
.B on
Rescan the PCI bus, clear a stale driver_override and rebind drivers. Root.
.TP
.B off
Run the safety checks, unbind snd_hda_intel then i915/xe, PCI-remove both. Root.
.TP
.B restore
Apply the saved state: switch off if the last \fBon\fR/\fBoff\fR was \fBoff\fR.
Run at boot by \fIarc-dgpu-ctl.service\fR. Root.
.TP
.B power
Power readings only (dGPU hwmon, CPU package RAPL, battery discharge).
.TP
.B diag
Troubleshooting dump.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH SAFETY CHECKS
\fBoff\fR refuses when no other display controller is active, when a monitor
is connected to the dGPU, when the dGPU is the firmware boot display, or when
the dGPU is bound to vfio-pci, audio is playing through its HDMI/DP codec, or
a process has work, memory or mapped buffers on the dGPU, or engine activity
is seen during a short sample. Holders are found by device number, including
processes in containers. Idle handles of Xorg, compositors, Xwayland,
plymouth, systemd-logind and PID 1 (\fBSESSION_HOLDERS\fR, system binaries
only, up to \fBSESSION_MEM_MAX\fR MiB), and handles that were only opened for
GPU enumeration, do not block. \fBFORCE=1\fR skips these checks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FORCE=1
Skip the safety checks on \fBoff\fR.
.TP
.B ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED=1
Allow Alchemist models that are not on the supported list.
.TP
.B PERSIST=0
Switch \fBon\fR/\fBoff\fR without changing the saved boot state.
.TP
.B VERBOSE=1
Log each step.
.TP
.B ARC_DGPU_CTL_CONF
Alternative configuration file (default \fI/etc/arc-dgpu-ctl.conf\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/arc-dgpu-ctl.conf
Optional PCI address and driver overrides.
.TP
.I arc-dgpu-ctl.service
systemd unit running \fBrestore\fR before the display manager. Enabled; does
nothing until \fBoff\fR has been run.
.TP
.I /var/lib/arc-dgpu-ctl/state
Saved state, \fBon\fR or \fBoff\fR.
.TP
.I 99-arc-dgpu-ctl.rules
udev rule that clears driver_override on Arc Alchemist devices.
.TP
.I /run/arc-dgpu-ctl.port
Cached PCIe port path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 error, 2 usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR udevadm (8)
